 "notes": [
  "Character construction follows the attack key (open coat tails over trousers); the neutral reference uses a closed coat-skirt - drift risk recorded at style lock.",
  "hero_turn clip's final frame faces left in the source art; the runtime flips the whole container with facing, giving a brief wrong-facing read mid-turn.",
  "All frames: green-screen sheets chroma-keyed programmatically (alpha from green dominance, despilled; per-sheet alpha coverage logged by the pipeline), one uniform anchor scale per actor (hero_idle/pursuer_idle/swooper_cruise/ranged_idle/boss_idle), fixed contract canvases and pivots, frames trimmed for atlasing with per-frame trim offsets restored at runtime (art/clips.json trims).",
  "CORRECTION (2026-10-09): the 'one uniform anchor scale per actor' statement in the note above did not hold in the shipped frames (hero walk 192 px vs idle 224 px; crouch 252 px; boss turn/hurt clipped at 448 px). Fixed by per-clip scale normalization; full before/after record in the scale_fix_2026_10_09 section of this manifest and game/art/SCALE_AUDIT_*.md.",
  "Atlases repacked 2026-10-09 after the scale fix: 5 pages / 80.0 MiB (was 7 / 112.0), still within the ratified R1 residency model (<= 7 pages, mips off).",
  "WHIP/VFX FIX (2026-10-09, user-reported): whip clips rebuilt as one continuous coil->unfurl->curved-crack->recoil motion per clip (procedural ribbon renderer, tools/fix_whip_vfx.py; handle plates pixel-identical, grip (276,~308) every frame, crack reach 172u); vfx_whip_impact rebuilt as a single-peak starburst envelope (peak 204px, center-locked); vfx_enemy_defeat growth/decay + radial feather; vfx_checkpoint_activate width dip smoothed; vfx_hazard_eruption tail re-widening repaired; vfx_hazard_telegraph art shifted +108px to sit on the ground at its spawn (was floating 58-88u up). Full before/after metrics: game/art/WHIP_VFX_FIX_2026-10-09.md. Originals archived in game/art/source/frames_prefix_2026-10-09.zip."
