 "scale_fix_2026_10_09": {
  "bug": "User report 2026-10-09: main character changes size while moving / standing still.",
  "root_cause": "Per-clip generation scale drift, propagated by the original pipeline's single per-actor anchor scale; several sheets also carried detached debris (thin sheet lines, specks) that inflated bounding boxes (e.g. frames measuring the full canvas height). The shipped note below claiming 'one uniform anchor scale per actor' was therefore wrong in effect; it is kept unedited as history and corrected here.",
  "method": "One uniform scale per clip (never per frame): scale = target / reference, the reference being a pose-aware statistic of the figure's largest-connected-component bbox heights measured on the green-screen source cells (median for upright clips, max for jump/fall/knockback extension, first-two-frames for knockdown/death openings, last frame for crouch_enter, min (most-grounded frame) for pursuer rear-up clips). Hero standing target 224 px (idle unchanged), crouch family 140 px (0.625 x 224, chosen for this fix). Frames placed by the LCC bbox (figure's lowest point on the contract pivot), and small detached debris components (area < 1% of the figure or min bbox side <= 6 px) removed and logged by the pipeline. Whip keeps its tip-reach rule on cleaned frames; grip still lands on the (276, 308) pivot (verified in SCALE_AUDIT_AFTER.md).",
  "audits": [
   "game/art/SCALE_AUDIT_BEFORE.md",
   "game/art/SCALE_AUDIT_AFTER.md",
   "game/tests/shots/scale_contact_sheet.png"
  ],
